1️⃣ First, confirm what actually exists locally
git branch


If you renamed locally using:

git branch -m old-name new-name


that only renames the local branch.

2️⃣ Check what exists on remote
git branch -r


You’ll probably still see:

origin/old-name


and not origin/new-name.

3️⃣ Push the renamed branch (this is the missing step)
git push origin new-name

4️⃣ Delete the old remote branch (important)
git push origin --delete old-name

5️⃣ Fix upstream tracking (people often forget this)
git branch --unset-upstream
git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/new-name


or in one shot:

git push --set-upstream origin new-name

6️⃣ If it still doesn’t reflect

Run:

git fetch --prune


This clears stale remote refs
